From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:10:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1328/3799] soh: rename func_80B93B68 ->
 ObjHsblock_InitDynaPoly

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: registers the block as a dyna-poly bg actor with the given collision header, warning when the bg actor table is full.
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Hsblock/z_obj_hsblock.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Hsblock/z_obj_hsblock.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Hsblock/z_obj_hsblock.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Hsblock/z_obj_hsblock.c
index 34606904b..bc1ed3928 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Hsblock/z_obj_hsblock.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Hsblock/z_obj_hsblock.c
@@ -53,7 +53,8 @@ void ObjHsblock_SetupAction(ObjHsblock* this, ObjHsblockActionFunc actionFunc) {
     this->actionFunc = actionFunc;
 }
 
-void func_80B93B68(ObjHsblock* this, PlayState* play, CollisionHeader* collision, s32 movementFlags) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80B93B68: registers the block as a dyna-poly bg actor with the given collision header, warning when the bg actor table is full.
+void ObjHsblock_InitDynaPoly(ObjHsblock* this, PlayState* play, CollisionHeader* collision, s32 movementFlags) {
     s32 pad;
     CollisionHeader* colHeader = NULL;
     s32 pad2[2];
@@ -78,7 +79,7 @@ void func_80B93BF0(ObjHsblock* this, PlayState* play) {
 void ObjHsblock_Init(Actor* thisx, PlayState* play) {
     ObjHsblock* this = (ObjHsblock*)thisx;
 
-    func_80B93B68(this, play, sCollisionHeaders[thisx->params & 3], DPM_UNK);
+    ObjHsblock_InitDynaPoly(this, play, sCollisionHeaders[thisx->params & 3], DPM_UNK);  // was func_80B93B68 [LLM:HIGH]
     Actor_ProcessInitChain(thisx, sInitChain);
     func_80B93BF0(this, play);
 
